    "post_quiz_faq_RG6RKB": {
      "type": "post-quiz-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_g8emjw": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Should I get both or a single set?",
            "answer": "<p>Most people order both, and the reason is straightforward: when your upper and lower are produced from the same impressions, the result reads as consistent and natural when you talk, laugh, or appear in a photo. A single set is a perfectly good option if you only want to address one. Either way, your set is built from your own impressions and nobody else's.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_bKnJUU": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens after I order?",
            "answer": "<p>Your impression kit ships within 48 hours, and everything you need is already inside the box, including a prepaid return label so that sending your impressions back costs you nothing. Once we receive your impressions, production of your set begins.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_wErC4m": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I cancel after ordering?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can cancel for a full refund at any point before production begins, because once we start building from your impressions, your set is already being made specifically and only for you, and that cannot be undone. Email support@reviveteeth.com and we will take care of everything from there.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_wJkaJp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long do they last?",
            "answer": "<p>How long your set holds up depends on how it is used and cared for, and I am not willing to make a durability promise that might not hold true for every person, because I think that kind of claim does you a disservice. What I will promise is two free remakes if something is not right when your set arrives, because that is a promise we can actually stand behind.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_wwix9B": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I wear them while eating?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, for everyday soft foods. Revive Veneers are made for daily wear, including eating and drinking. For hard, crunchy, sticky, or very hot foods, take them out first. They are a cosmetic appliance, not a replacement for your natural bite, so they are not built for heavy chewing. Removing them for tougher meals also helps them last longer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_9B4taA": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if they don't feel right?",
            "answer": "<p>Then we make it right. Your set was made to your mouth, so if it is off, that is our responsibility and not yours. We remake it free, up to twice, with prepaid shipping both ways, and a full refund is available any time before production begins. Email support@reviveteeth.com and we handle everything from there.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
